WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.215
Detections should be reviewed over time.

2
00:00:02.215 --> 00:00:14.029
Useful metrics may include alert volume, true positive rate, false positive patterns, analyst feedback, coverage relevance, investigation outcomes, and time spent on triage.

3
00:00:14.029 --> 00:00:15.845
Metrics should support decisions.

4
00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:22.829
They help teams identify which detections need tuning, better documentation, improved enrichment, or deeper review.

5
00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:32.767
Some detections should be retired because the threat is no longer relevant, telemetry changed, another detection replaced it, or the noise outweighs the value.

6
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:37.407
Retiring detections is part of maintaining a healthy detection portfolio.

7
00:00:37.407 --> 00:00:41.308
It keeps the signal set focused, understandable, and useful.
